      "answer_retrieved": true,
      "review": "The answer classifies 재미있다/맛있다/멋있다 as adjectives despite adnominal 는. It describes intention attachment as normatively verbal, while acknowledging actual 재미있으려고 with a state-making interpretation. It declines a categorical analysis because theories differ. This does not license every adjective in every context, or justify blanket removal.",
      "direct_surface_tokens": [
        "재미있으려고"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nikl:adj2003",
      "url": "https://www.korean.go.kr/nkview/nklife/2003_2/2003_0212.pdf",
      "title": "형용사",
      "author": "유현경",
      "publication": "새국어생활 13(2), 2003 summer",
      "pdf_sha256": "11a7680274858c63679fec829fee5a7d2e684f13b0216844c14d044ee955bd37",
      "locator": "Printed pages 192–193 (existential verbal/adjectival distinction) and 197 (intention connective restrictions).",
      "review": "The article distinguishes verbal human-stay 있다 from adjectival possession/existence and describes adjective restrictions on purpose/intention connectives. This supports independent homonym assessment, not transferring a verb entry’s evidence to its adjective homonym. The 2026 consultation supplies additional uncertainty for state-making uses."
    }
